From ff4349aee076bf2476e92cdd9b2b5c8bc7ed8b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:29:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] Progressive RADAR / CONFIRMING / READY detection across
 all three scanners

Step 8 of the Cross-Scanner Eligibility and Corporate Lifecycle Sprint.

The problem
-----------
When every criterion is compulsory from the first pass, a scanner can only find
mature setups and structurally cannot see a move beginning. V3 showed this
plainly: it loaded prices at min_sessions=260, so a stock with 150 sessions was
invisible however strongly it was moving, and it rejected 1,522 of 2,157 symbols
-- mostly on liquidity and delivery thresholds a stock satisfies only *after*
participation has already expanded.

The fix separates three questions that were collapsed into one:

  RADAR       Is something starting?          flexible
  CONFIRMING  Is the participation genuine?   moderate
  READY       May we authorise an entry?      strict

Nothing about READY is relaxed. Entry authorisation still requires the full
260-session strict pass, so entry quality is unchanged; only visibility below it
improves.

Added v2/progressive_stages.py
------------------------------
Shared *vocabulary and progression only* -- no strategy logic, so each scanner
keeps its own independent rules and thresholds. Score bands follow the
specification (35-49 radar, 50-64 confirming, 65+ qualified, 70+ ready).
Availability states (CIRCUIT_WATCH, CIRCUIT_LOCKED, POST_CIRCUIT_CONFIRMING,
EXTENDED, CORPORATE_REVIEW, TERMINATED, OBSERVE_ONLY) sit *beside* the
progression rather than inside it, so a circuit-locked or merged symbol is
displayed with its score intact and simply cannot be entered -- NHCFOODS is
detected even when it cannot be bought. A score is never an authorisation: a
symbol scoring 95 with an outstanding gate is held at QUALIFIED.

Added v2/tiered_eligibility.py
------------------------------
Reuses evaluate_eligibility unchanged, run at three tiers strictest-first:

  READY            260 sessions, verified market cap and promoter holding
  CONFIRMING       180 sessions, turnover and delivery confirmation
  DISCOVERY_RADAR  120 sessions, liquidity floor only, card says DATA PENDING

Relaxation is not a loophole: NON_EQ_SERIES and RESTRICTED_SECURITY reject at
every tier, which is asserted.

Wiring
------
* V3 loads the universe at MIN_TIER_SESSIONS instead of 260 -- otherwise RADAR
  is unreachable by construction. run_daily gains progressive_stages=True,
  stage_funnel, radar_symbols and confirming_symbols, and the admin message
  gains a PROGRESSIVE FUNNEL section naming what holds symbols below READY.
* Momentum Ladder: surviving discovery ranking is CONFIRMING, full Hull
  alignment is QUALIFIED, alignment plus entry permission is READY.
* Hull Pine: its own BUILD -> NEAR -> READY -> TRIGGERED -> ENTERED lifecycle
  mapped onto the shared stages; overextended symbols carry the EXTENDED
  availability state instead of vanishing.

Measured on the real store at 2026-08-20, V3 now surfaces 208 symbols that were
previously entirely absent from its output:

  READY 713 | CONFIRMING 185 | RADAR 23
  held below READY by: LOW_MEDIAN_VOLUME 652, LOW_PRICE 356,
                       INSUFFICIENT_HISTORY 251, LOW_MEDIAN_TURNOVER 146

The 23 RADAR names are mostly recent listings -- AMAGI, FRACTAL, ARIS, AYE,
CLEANMAX, ALGOQUANT, ANTELOPUS -- young movers with under 260 sessions, which is
precisely the population the old funnel could not see.

Tests: 48 new. Suite 360 passed; the same 7 pre-existing Telegram copy-text
failures as on main.
